command-description-ksoffset-local =
    Offsets each piped entity's local position by a vector, e.g. 'ksoffset:local [1, -2.5]'. The offset is in the entity's parent's frame, so on a grid it follows that grid's rotation. Anchored entities are unanchored, moved, and re-anchored onto the tile they land on.
command-description-ksoffset-world =
    Offsets each piped entity's world position by a vector, e.g. 'ksoffset:world [1, -2.5]'. The offset is in map space no matter what the entity is parented to. Anchored entities are unanchored, moved, and re-anchored onto the tile they land on.
